// Thessaly Hollow (bible 4.7, 7.3 steps 2–3; character-bibles.md §5, §8). The Lantern (Hollow_1): inside, colour
// blooming round Wren, and a grey chick starts following. The Hollow (Hollow_2): Ilse, grey, sees her first
// (reveal 5.3). Isolde, alive, grey at the edges, cannot leave under her own power.
// Ilse: lets go; sees Wren before Wren sees her; does not say "stay". She does not name her daughter: the name
// is Isolde's gift, and Ilse never had it. Isolde here is proud ("journeyman"), not scared.
// Marrow echoes; its first original word is a word no one in the Hollow says.

title: Hollow_Ilse
---
<<if has_flag("blank.ilse.heard")>>
    Ilse: Go and see my father. Then come and sit with me, if there's time. #still #face:bright #line:00e534c
    <<stop>>
<<endif>>
Ilse: There you are. I saw you at the edge of the village before you saw me. #face:bright #line:09cad43
Ilse: You hold your head the same. Tilted, as if you're listening for something far off. #face:bright #line:04cad9d
Ilse: You were born here. After. When the Hollow was already like this. #reveal:5.3 #line:01a80d7
Ilse: Children born in the white belong to both. You could see her. The woman with the lantern. #line:0517bd8
Ilse: She carried you out. The crossing took everything you remembered. I let it. #face:grave #line:0a7cae8
Ilse: I let you go. It was the only thing I was ever sure of. #face:grave #line:0a6ae91
-> You're my mother. #line:0babe80
    Ilse: I was. I am. It's the same word here. #face:grave #line:0d0d613
    <<voice surveyor blank>>
-> Come out with me. #line:0b4c11f
    Ilse: No. I let go of things. It's what I'm good at. #face:grave #line:071d3c7
    <<voice warden blank>>
-> ... #line:0b0133e
    Ilse: You did that as a chick too. Looked, and said nothing. #face:bright #line:06cbed0
    <<voice drift blank>>
Ilse: My father holds this place. He held on too hard, once. Ask him what it cost. #plant:5.4 #face:grave #line:06f0221
Ilse: Take this. The Remnant's charter. Grey is a colour you can carry. #line:06c7b70
<<charter Remnant>>
<<flag blank.ilse.heard 1>>
===

title: Hollow_Isolde
---
<<if has_flag("blank.isolde.found")>>
    <<if has_flag("keystone.isolde")>>
        Isolde: Go on, journeyman. I'm not going anywhere. That's the problem. #still #line:0579e5c
    <<else>>
        Isolde: Still carrying his stone. The sixth slot's. Want it now? #still #line:08debfb
        -> I'll carry it. #line:0c9627b
            <<voice warden blank>>
            Isolde: Heavier than it looks. Don't tell Teodor I said that. He'll say it first. #face:bright #line:0187126
            <<flag keystone.isolde 1>>
        -> Not yet. #line:0da1d1e
            <<voice surveyor blank>>
            Isolde: Stubborn. Good. #still #face:bright #line:0bd177c
    <<endif>>
    <<stop>>
<<endif>>
Isolde: Journeyman. You crossed. Look at you. #face:bright #line:02450ea
Isolde: I can't leave. I tried. The white lets go of things that walked in whole. I didn't. #face:grave #line:0a36a4a
Isolde: Did you read it? The atlas? Then you know what I took, and who it's for. #face:asking #line:0dce774
-> I read it. All of it. #line:04da2e7
    Isolde: Good. Then you don't need me to explain. You never did. #face:bright #line:0b14509
    <<voice surveyor blank>>
-> I'm getting you out. #line:0429857
    Isolde: No carrying. Finish what you came for. Then we'll see what's left to carry. #face:wary #line:0f4ea8c
    <<voice warden blank>>
-> ... #line:04d451e
    Isolde: That's mine. You stole that from me. Keep it. #face:bright #line:00aff0d
    <<voice drift blank>>
Isolde: And this. The sixth slot's stone. Corvin's. I never got it to him. #face:grave #line:09fc704
-> I'll carry it. #line:0dd64c9
    <<voice warden blank>>
    Isolde: Heavier than it looks. Don't tell Teodor I said that. He'll say it first. #face:bright #line:06da2fe
    <<flag keystone.isolde 1>>
-> Keep it. Give it him yourself. #line:06ed433
    <<voice drift blank>>
    Isolde: Stubborn. Good. I'll hold it, then. #face:bright #line:003023d
<<flag blank.isolde.found 1>>
===

title: Blank_Marrow_Follow
---
<<if not has_flag("marrow.following")>>
    Lantern: White, and then colour, blooming round her feet as she walks. #line:0d0fc19
    Lantern: An island drifts up under her. Behind her, one pace back and one to the left, a grey chick. #line:020168b
    <<flag marrow.following 1>>
    <<stop>>
<<endif>>
<<if has_flag("blank.ilse.heard") and flag("marrow.words") < 1>>
    Ilse: I let you go. It was the only thing I was ever sure of. #face:grave #line:0e883ae
    Marrow: Let you go. #echo:ilse #line:00873a0
    Marrow: Wren. #line:019f062
    <<flag marrow.words 1>>
    <<stop>>
<<endif>>
Lantern: The grey chick, one pace back, one to the left. #still #line:0264402
===
